We had a discussion about the overpoweredness of wishing last summer;
my preferred solution was:

* Wands of wishing cannot be recharged.
* Wands of wishing cannot have the last zap wrested from them.
* The Castle wand is guaranteed to be 0:3.
* Randomly-generated wands of wishing are random from 0:1 to 0:3, as
  at present.

I think this is a better approach to wish-inflation than removing them
entirely from the rest of the game; you _should_ be able to find a
wand of wishing in the first room of DL1, go "Woo-hoo!", and YASD two
levels down. The game wouldn't be the same without it.

